{"year":"2026","content":[{"type":"text","content_text":"The 79th Cannes Film Festival took place from May 12 to 23, 2026, with South Korea's <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 10099, 'screen_type': person}\">Park Chan-wook</a> as jury president. Romania's <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 20657, 'screen_type': person}\">Cristian Mungiu</a> won his second Palme d'Or with <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 1401459, 'screen_type': movie}\">Fjord</a> (2026), after <i>4 Months, 3 Weeks and 2 Days</i> (2007). The directing prize ended in a tie between the duo Javier Calvo and Javier Ambrossi, for <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 1422041, 'screen_type': movie}\">La bola negra</a> (2026), and <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 64194, 'screen_type': person}\">Paweł Pawlikowski</a>, for <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 1437696, 'screen_type': movie}\">Ojczyzna</a> (Fatherland, 2026), and the acting prizes were shared by pairs of actresses and actors. Peter Jackson, Barbra Streisand and John Travolta received honorary Palmes d'Or."},{"type":"person_list","title":"The Jury","persons":[{"id":10099,"name":"Park Chan-wook","profile_path":"/jsSFCVB7MhuVbSLwTgESiXEiNjt.jpg"},{"id":2021353,"name":"Diego Céspedes","profile_path":"/75zokW0mjTj2BUayXKp0rGHaQVB.jpg"},{"id":4812,"name":"Isaach de Bankolé","profile_path":"/aGjABQBgTA3tduuh54hzWx0aQ44.jpg"},{"id":15490,"name":"Paul Laverty","profile_path":"/94iBo0p6XMgtkK6OOLMzKuaHT4G.jpg"},{"id":3416,"name":"Demi Moore","profile_path":"/wApParZYBDi4yxekjfxjKEifJYh.jpg"},{"id":17018,"name":"Ruth Negga","profile_path":"/eUnSUgbD050mKSCqOJvXplAiF9S.jpg"},{"id":1640,"name":"Stellan Skarsgård","profile_path":"/mW7xmtGV4y79kQGn0zkKVGDMAmw.jpg"},{"id":1319437,"name":"Laura Wandel","profile_path":"/wn1zsTTQEyQmMO3Fq7M6SMmk6X5.jpg"},{"id":1395183,"name":"Chloé Zhao","profile_path":"/r8DmTdOqHbDUydCOVb277rncPTK.jpg"}]},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Palme d'Or","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":1